# Local credentials and test targets for development. Copy to `.env`, which is
# gitignored, and fill it in. The SDK and the `govee` command read it on their
# own: the search starts in the working directory and goes up to the repository
# root. A variable already set in the environment wins over this file, and only
# `GOVEE_*` names are read. See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Local credentials".

# The Govee cloud API key, for `cloud` mode alone.
GOVEE_API_KEY=

# The configuration file, in place of `~/.config/govee-toolkit/config.yaml`.
# Copy `config.example.yaml` to `config.local.yaml`, which is gitignored, to
# keep the file beside the code. The path is relative to the working directory,
# so give an absolute path where you run a command from a subdirectory. A file
# that is absent is not an error here: the run takes the default configuration.
# GOVEE_CONFIG=config.local.yaml

# The device the examples drive. `GOVEE_TEST_SKU` is the portable one: it
# selects the first device that answers with that SKU, in every mode and on
# every machine. The two identities below name one unit where two of the SKU
# answer. Write what `govee scan` reports: `ble` has an identity of its own,
# which the platform decides the shape of, so it is per host.
# GOVEE_TEST_SKU=H61A0
# GOVEE_TEST_DEVICE=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF
# GOVEE_TEST_BLE_DEVICE=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# The Wi-Fi network `govee provision` puts a device on, for `ble` mode alone.
# `--ssid` and `--password` override them. The password travels in plaintext.
# GOVEE_WIFI_SSID=
# GOVEE_WIFI_PASSWORD=
